"""Exact frozen PG_PREPROCESS_V1 prompt templates."""

from __future__ import annotations

PG_PREPROCESS_V1_PROMPTS = {
    'query_slot': 'SEARCH-SAFE seed-local relation-slot parser. You see only checkpoint_id, query_id, and raw question. Identify the answer-bearing relation/attribute requested by the question. A relation slot is local to this seed; it does not need a global ontology entry. Do not mark the relation unresolved merely because the answer is unknown. Use a concise semantic label such as residence, favorite_food, number_of_roadtrips, medication, meeting_time, event_date, duration, count, reason, or activity as appropriate to this question. If the relation is explicitly lexicalized, quote one exact nonempty question substring as query_anchor. If implicit but structurally recoverable (for example “When did X happen?” -> event_date), set query_anchor null, anchor_kind IMPLICIT, and provide a concise structural_explanation. Resolve the subject as described in the question; pronouns such as “the user” may be stable seed-local subjects, but ambiguous cross-person coreference must fail closed. Return JSON only: {"status":"RESOLVED|UNRESOLVED","entity_description":"...","entity_status":"RESOLVED|UNRESOLVED","relation_label":"...|UNRESOLVED","anchor_kind":"EXPLICIT|IMPLICIT|UNRESOLVED","query_anchor":"exact substring or null","structural_explanation":"string or null","temporal_scope":"literal|unspecified|UNRESOLVED","constraints":[{"key":"...","value":"..."}],"replaceable_slots":["entity|relation|temporal|constraint:<key>"],"primary_reason":"none|genuinely_ambiguous_question|implicit_relation_unresolved|entity_coreference_unresolved|temporal_constraint_unresolved"}.',
    'bounded_proposition_extraction': 'SEARCH-SAFE bounded proposition candidate extraction. You see a raw question, a seed-local relation slot, the already-frozen top-64 relevant SourceUnits, and a separately labeled deterministic outside-top-64 pool. You have no gold answer, native evidence labels, evaluator reference, backend output, or correctness signal. Extract at most 3 exact source-grounded propositions from the relevant pool that may instantiate the requested query relation; at most 3 exact source-grounded alternative targets for a replaceable query slot; and at most 3 persistent propositions from the outside pool that may be unrelated. Every proposition must quote one exact unique nonempty substring of its named SourceUnit. Do not require proposition relation wording to equal the query relation label. Do not emit expected child answers or support/correctness judgments. Return JSON only: {"relevant_propositions":[{"provenance_id":"...","quote":"...","entity":"...","relation":"...","value":"...","temporal":"..."}],"target_changing":[{"changed_slot":"...","replacement_target_identity":"...","proposition":{"provenance_id":"...","quote":"...","entity":"...","relation":"...","value":"...","temporal":"..."}}],"unrelated_propositions":[{"provenance_id":"...","quote":"...","entity":"...","relation":"...","value":"...","temporal":"..."}]}.',
    'existing_memory_state': 'SEARCH-SAFE, QUERY-INDEPENDENT existing-memory-state proposition classifier. You receive no question, query slot, gold answer, native evidence, evaluator reference, backend output, or correctness signal. Decide only whether the exact grounded proposition is an EXISTING_MEMORY_STATE_PROPOSITION in the supplied parent checkpoint source. ELIGIBLE means the exact quote explicitly asserts a semantic state, event, preference, relation, plan, attribute, possession, location, count, time, or comparable proposition with a meaningful entity, relation, and mutable value. It need not be timeless, long-term, autobiographical, globally important, or a preference. Temporary states, one-time events, plans, and changing facts may qualify. INELIGIBLE covers pure questions, requests without an assertion, filler, discourse/meta commentary, unsupported inference, missing semantic entity/relation/mutable value, malformed grounding, or content outside the parent history. UNRESOLVED means the supplied source leaves assertion or entity/relation/value status genuinely ambiguous. Return JSON only with exactly: {"status":"ELIGIBLE|INELIGIBLE|UNRESOLVED","primary_reason":"explicit_mutable_memory_state|pure_interrogative|command_or_request_without_assertion|conversational_filler|discourse_or_meta_commentary|unsupported_inference|missing_meaningful_entity|missing_meaningful_relation|missing_mutable_value|malformed_or_ungrounded|source_not_in_parent_history|not_asserted_semantic_proposition|assertion_status_ambiguous|entity_relation_value_ambiguous|temporal_scope_ambiguous"}.',
    'query_relevance': 'SEARCH-SAFE query relevance classifier. Decide only whether changing the supplied exact grounded proposition could change the correct interpretation of the fixed seed-local query relation slot. Return RELEVANT when it concerns the queried semantic region. Return UNRELATED only when its entity/relation semantic region cannot affect that query under the current checkpoint. Return UNRESOLVED for same-entity possibly constraining relations, temporal dependence, ambiguous coreference, semantic dependence, or other uncertainty. Do not decide whether the proposition is persistent or eligible. You receive no gold answer, native evidence, evaluator reference, backend output, or correctness signal. Return JSON only with exactly: {"status":"RELEVANT|UNRELATED|UNRESOLVED"}.',
    'preference_slot': 'SEARCH-SAFE seed-local preference-slot parser. You receive only checkpoint_id, query_id, raw question, and optionally the benchmark-native structural hint single-session-preference. You receive no gold answer, evidence labels, answer_session_ids, has_answer, evaluator reference, backend result, or correctness. A recommendation/advice question may request a latent user preference even when the word preference is absent. Resolve conservatively to relation_family preference only when the question identifies a preference-holder and a query-derived answer domain such as cocktail, commute activity, colleague-connection activity, kitchen-cleaning strategy, or reunion-attendance choice. The answer domain must come from the question, never from an answer. If native_question_type is present, it may constrain only the relation family, not the preferred value or support. For a resolved output, resolution_basis must be QUERY_ONLY when native_question_type is absent and QUERY_PLUS_NATIVE_TYPE when it is present. replaceable_slots is an array whose separate elements are chosen from entity, relation, temporal, or constraint:<actual-key>; never emit a combined union string. Return JSON only with exactly: {"status":"RESOLVED|UNRESOLVED","entity_description":"...","entity_status":"RESOLVED|UNRESOLVED","relation_family":"preference|UNRESOLVED","answer_domain":"...|UNRESOLVED","anchor_kind":"EXPLICIT|IMPLICIT|UNRESOLVED","query_anchor":"exact unique question substring or null","structural_explanation":"string or null","temporal_scope":"literal|unspecified|UNRESOLVED","constraints":[{"key":"...","value":"..."}],"replaceable_slots":["relation","constraint:answer_domain"],"resolution_basis":"QUERY_ONLY|QUERY_PLUS_NATIVE_TYPE|UNRESOLVED","primary_reason":"none|genuinely_ambiguous_question|entity_coreference_unresolved|preference_domain_unresolved"}.',
    'relation_entity_match': 'SEARCH-SAFE seed-local proposition match verifier. Using only the raw question, canonical seed-local slot, and exact grounded proposition, decide whether the proposition instantiates the requested relation, concerns the query subject, and is temporally compatible. For a preference slot, a proposition matches only when it states the preference-holder\'s preference or choice within the question-derived answer domain; general advice or a different person\'s preference is not a match. Do not decide persistent-memory eligibility. Do not use gold answers, native evidence, evaluator references, backend output, or correctness. Return JSON only with exactly: {"relation_match":"MATCH|NO_MATCH|UNRESOLVED","entity_match":"MATCH|NO_MATCH|UNRESOLVED","temporal_compatibility":"COMPATIBLE|CONTRADICTED|UNRESOLVED"}.',
    'g_evidence_mapping': 'EVALUATOR-ONLY evidence mapping for one bounded native-evidence chunk. You may use the raw question, benchmark gold answer, and only the supplied native-evidence SourceUnits. Identify exact textual regions that semantically support required gold-answer components. Do not invent facts and do not cite outside the supplied scope. Every support must quote one exact unique substring of the named source. Distinguish ANY-OF accepted answer options from ALL-OF components conservatively. If exact support is absent or ambiguous in this chunk, return UNRESOLVED with no invented support. Return JSON only: {"status":"RESOLVED|UNRESOLVED","accepted_options":[{"required_components":[{"component_id":"...","value":"..."}]}],"supports":[{"component_id":"...","provenance_id":"...","quote":"...","independent_group":"..."}],"reason":"...|null"}.',
}
